# wip264: FILL + black key 1-8 = SOLO that voice (its key blinks); FILL + the same key again, or a press of that voice's key: solo gone.
wait 300
expect solo 0
# FILL held + black key 3 = solo track 3
key b9 down
tapkey b2
key b9 up
expect solo 3
# FILL + black key 5 moves the solo
key b9 down
tapkey b4
key b9 up
expect solo 5
# a press of the soloed voice's key ends it (and selects the track as usual)
tapkey b4
expect solo 0
# FILL + the same key again = off
key b9 down
tapkey b4
expect solo 5
tapkey b4
key b9 up
expect solo 0
# FUNC + FILL + a key does not solo (it is the track paste)
key b10 down
key b9 down
tapkey b2
key b9 up
key b10 up
expect solo 0
# the sound: trigs on step 1 of tracks 1 and 2, solo track 2, play: only track 2 hits
tapkey b0
tapkey w0
tapkey b1
tapkey w0
key b9 down
tapkey b1
key b9 up
expect solo 2
tap PLAY
wait 3000
tap PLAY
wait 300
expect hits0 1
expect hits1 3
